<.page_title
  title="Benchmark suites"
  subtitle="The built-in, versioned scenario suites that workspace benchmark runs execute. This catalog is generated from the shipped suite fixtures, so it always matches what the runner and CLI offer."
/>

<div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>What built-in suites are</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Built-in suites are reusable, versioned templates shipped with ControlKeel. Every workspace
      runs the same fixtures, so results are comparable across workspaces and across subjects. You
      cannot edit or create built-in suites from the product — they change only with ControlKeel
      versions, and each suite records its version number so old runs stay attributable.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Run them from your workspace's
      <a href={~p"/docs"} class="text-primary hover:underline">Benchmarks</a> page, or from the CLI
      with <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">controlkeel obs benchmarks run --suite &lt;slug&gt;</code>.
      External agent hosts (OpenCode, Copilot, Claude, Codex, Gemini) join the comparison through
      <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">manual_import</code> or
      <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">shell</code> subjects configured in
      <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">controlkeel/benchmark_subjects.json</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <.section_title>Suite catalog</.section_title>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <%= for suite <- @suites do %>
        <article id={"docs-suite-#{suite.slug}"} class="rounded-xl border bg-muted/20 p-4 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground/90">{suite.name}</h3>
            <span class="inline-flex shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">
              v{suite.version}
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs leading-6 text-muted-foreground">{suite.description}</p>
          <dl class="space-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
            <div class="flex gap-2">
              <dt class="font-medium text-foreground/80 shrink-0">Slug</dt>
              <dd><code class="font-mono">{suite.slug}</code></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-2">
              <dt class="font-medium text-foreground/80 shrink-0">Scenarios</dt>
              <dd>{length(suite.scenarios)}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-2">
              <dt class="font-medium text-foreground/80 shrink-0">Domains</dt>
              <dd>
                <%= case ControlKeel.Benchmark.domain_packs_for_suite(suite) do %>
                  <% [] -> %>
                    All suite scenarios
                  <% packs -> %>
                    {Enum.map_join(packs, ", ", &ControlKeel.Intent.pack_label/1)}
                <% end %>
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-border/50 space-y-1">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground">
              Scenarios
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-0.5">
              <%= for scenario <- Enum.sort_by(suite.scenarios, & &1.position) do %>
                <li class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                  <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">{scenario.slug}</code>
                  — {scenario.name}
                </li>
              <% end %>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <.section_title>Reading a run</.section_title>
    <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      A benchmark run pairs every scenario with every selected subject and scores deterministic
      policy decisions: catch rate, block rate, expected-rule hit rate, and overhead. Multi-subject
      runs also produce a subject comparison with deltas against the baseline subject. Keep external
      claims bounded to the suite slug, version, scenario count, subjects, and scorer — see
      <code class="font-mono text-foreground/80">docs/benchmarks.md</code> for the claim discipline.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
